motions.source_motion_text:
THAT Council adopt “City of Langford 2026-2030 Financial Plan Bylaw No. 2281, 2026”;
               AND
               "City of Langford Tax Rates Bylaw No. 2282, 2026".

THAT Council close the meeting to the public pursuant to section 90 (1) (e), (g) and (i) of the
       Community Charter to consider:

           •   the acquisition, disposition or expropriation of land or improvements;

           •   litigation or potential litigation affecting the municipality;

           •   the receipt of advice that is subject to solicitor-client privilege, including
               communications necessary for that purpose.

THAT Council take no action with respect to this application to rezone 728
        Massie Drive and 2746 Dinan Place under Bylaw No. 2097 until such time as the
        following items are addressed and reviewed by the Sustainable Development
        Advisory Committee:

            a. Substantial completion of the proposed development concept, including
               the commercial opportunities;

            b. Surface parking for any commercial opportunities;

            c. Water table depth;

            d. Bicycle parking and alternative transportation opportunities; and

            e. Early Guidance Guidelines for development be utilized.

THAT Council adopt "Animal Control Miscellaneous Amending Bylaw No. 2212, 2026";

             AND

             THAT Council adopt "Animal Responsibility Bylaw No. 2239, 2026".

THAT Council adopt “Community Standards Bylaw No. 2255, 2026”;
       AND
       “Community Standards Miscellaneous Amending Bylaw, No. 2262, 2026”.

THAT Council consider giving first reading to Bylaw 2031 as drafted;

           AND

           THAT Council direct staff to host an information session with members of the
           development community and public to establish DP Area Climate Action parameters
           prior to bringing forward draft DP guidelines for Council's review;

WHEREAS the position of CRD Director is one of significant regional governance and
           impact;
           AND WHEREAS having a process for the public to provide input aligns with Priority Five
           of the Strategic Plan: Good Governance, increasing transparency and promoting
           democratic values;
           AND WHEREAS allowing public input on a preference for this position is standard
           practice in other municipalities with more than one CRD Director position;

                THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council direct staff to prepare a report on what the
                process would be to include an expression of preference for CRD Director as part of the
                2026 election.

THAT Council adopt "Amenity Cost Charge Bylaw No. 2275, 2026";
             AND
             THAT Council adopt "Inclusionary Zoning Bylaw No. 2270, 2026";
             AND
             THAT Council adopt “City of Langford Reserve Funds Establishment Bylaw, 2004, Bylaw
             No. 857, Amendment No. 3, Bylaw No. 2271, 2026”.

THAT Council:

        1.   Proceed with the consideration of the temporary use permit for a
             commercial office at 2874 Peatt Road, subject to the following terms and
             conditions:

             i.    That the temporary use permit be issued for a period of three years
                   from time of issuance;

             ii.   That there are no clients on site;

             iii. That a business licence and building permit be obtained from the City of
                  Langford;

THAT Council consider the following as policing priorities for the West Shore RCMP in
             2025:

                 •      Police presence in the community including attention to the unhoused
                        population;
                 •      Drug issues;
                 •      Addressing concerns regarding gangs;
                 •      Youth issues;
                 •      Mental health
                 •      Traffic;
                 •      Property crime and theft;
                 •      Cybercrime;
                 •      Online fraud; and
                 •      Social media driven issues particularly those affecting youth.

